{"status":"question","question":{"text":"Great — a budget & expense tracker you and your partner both use, seeded from bank CSV. Before features, this first mission is just the foundation: a booting skeleton, a real test runner a human can watch run, and one thin slice that proves they're wired together. First decision — the stack. I'd recommend **Vite + React + Vitest**: it boots to something on screen fast (you'll want charts and tables later), Vitest gives you a real runner you can watch go green, and it's a browser app you and your partner can both open. Does that fit, or did you picture something else (a desktop app, plain server-rendered, a different language)?","choices":["Vite + React + Vitest (recommended)","Something else — desktop app","Something else — server-rendered / different language","Let me describe it"],"recommended":"Vite + React + Vitest","closing":false},"prd":"# Mission: Foundation — Budget & Expense Tracker skeleton\n\n**Type:** feature\n**Goal:** Stand up a booting skeleton, a working test runner, and one thin vertical slice proving both are connected — the foundation for a personal budget & expense tracker.\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\n- The project boots and shows something on screen.\n- A real test runner is wired and can be watched running by a human.\n- One thin vertical slice proves skeleton + tests are genuinely connected.\n**Out of Scope:**\n- Budgets, charts, bank sync (deferred to later missions).\n- Full categorisation engine, multi-user accounts.\n**Constraints:**\n- Stack: TBD (pending captain confirmation).\n\n## Deferred features (project vision)\n- Budgets\n- Charts / spending visualisations\n- Bank sync\n- Transaction categorisation\n- Shared use for two people (captain + partner)"}

